Q9. "How are ACID properties enforced in your Zaika MySQL database?"
Answer:
- Atomicity: All steps of placing an order or settling a split bill succeed together inside db.commit() or roll back completely via db.rollback() on any error.
- Consistency: Foreign keys, NOT NULL constraints, CHECK (quantity >= 1), and ENUM statuses prevent invalid database states.
- Isolation: Row-level locking (.with_for_update()) isolates concurrent split-bill payments so they do not overwrite each other.
- Durability: Once committed to MySQL, paid bills and closed orders persist safely even if the backend container restarts.

